{"attribution":"Federal Emergency Management Agency, Ready.gov, Landslides and Debris Flow, Simplified Chinese; no FEMA, DHS, or U.S. Government endorsement or affiliation is implied.","cases":[{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-001","input":"山体滑坡发生在美国所有州和地区，可能由许多因素引起，包括地震、风暴、火山爆发、火灾和土地的人为改造。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-001","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-002","input":"最危险、最危及生命和最致命的山体滑坡是那些发生得很快的山体滑坡，通常很少有人注意到。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-002","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-003","input":"当大量的岩石、泥土或碎片沿着斜坡移动时，就会发生山体滑坡。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-003","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-004","input":"当野火烧毁斜坡时，会在数年内增加山体滑坡的可能性。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-004","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-005","input":"如何保护您自己或您的财产取决于滑坡的类型。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-005","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-006","input":"土地利用分区、专业检查和适当的设计可以减少许多滑坡问题，但疏散通常是保护生命免受泥石流或其他快速移动的滑坡伤害的唯一方法。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-006","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-007","input":"并非所有的山体滑坡都很快。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-007","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-008","input":"一些缓慢移动的山体滑坡以蜗牛的速度移动，停止和开始，并且每年前进不超过三英尺。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-008","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-009","input":"虽然这些山体滑坡很少造成人员伤亡，但随着时间的推移，它们会对土地和财产造成破坏。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-009","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-010","input":"制定一个计划，包括您的宠物，以便您和您的家人知道在发生山体滑坡时该做什么以及该去哪里。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-010","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-011","input":"注册您社区的警告系统。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-011","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-012","input":"紧急警报系统(EAS)和美国国家海洋和大气管理局(NOAA)天气广播也提供紧急警报。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-012","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-013","input":"如果您被告知要撤离，或者您觉得留在家里不安全，请离开。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-013","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-014","input":"将SHELTER + 您的邮政编码发送至43362( 4FEMA )，以查找您所在地区最近的避难所（例如：避难所 12345）。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-014","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-015","input":"请咨询专业人士，了解适合您的家庭或企业的预防措施，例如可以更好地抵抗破裂的柔性管件。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-015","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-016","input":"根据合格岩土工程专家的建议和/或当地市/县关于防止泥石流和洪水的指南保护您的财产。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-016","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-017","input":"您无法阻止或改变泥石流的路径。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-017","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-018","input":"但是，您可以使用沙袋、挡土墙或k-rails（泽西护栏）来保护您的财产免受洪水或泥浆的侵袭。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-018","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-019","input":"在泥石流地区，考虑建造渠道或偏转墙以尝试引导建筑物周围的流动。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-019","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-020","input":"但是请注意，当流量足够大时，它会流向它喜欢的地方。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-020","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-021","input":"此外，如果您转移流量并流向邻居的财产，您可能需要承担损害赔偿责任。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-021","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-022","input":"如果您面临山体滑坡的风险，请咨询您的保险代理人。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-022","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-023","input":"国家洪水保险计划(NFIP)的洪水保险政策可能涵盖泥石流。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-023","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-024","input":"如果您在野火燃烧区附近，请注册紧急警报并注意燃烧区的天气预报。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-024","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-025","input":"聆听并注意是否有湍急的水流、泥浆或异常的声音。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-025","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-026","input":"不寻常的声音，如树木开裂或巨石撞击在一起，可能表明有移动的碎片。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-026","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-027","input":"随着山体滑坡的临近，可以注意到音量逐渐增大的微弱隆隆声。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-027","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-028","input":"景观中的巨石可能是过去泥石流的迹象。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-028","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-029","input":"您的景观会发生变化，例如斜坡上的雨水排放模式（尤其是径流汇集的地方）、陆地运动、小滑坡、水流或逐渐倾斜的树木。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-029","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-030","input":"门或窗第一次粘住或卡住。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-030","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-031","input":"灰泥、瓷砖、砖块或地基出现新裂缝。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-031","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-032","input":"外墙、人行道或楼梯开始远离建筑物。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-032","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-033","input":"地面或街道或车道等铺砌区域出现缓慢发展、扩大的裂缝。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-033","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-034","input":"地下公用事业线路断裂。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-034","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-035","input":"隆起的地面出现在斜坡的底部。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-035","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-036","input":"水在新位置冲破地表。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-036","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-037","input":"栅栏、挡土墙、电线杆或树木倾斜或移动。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-037","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-038","input":"地面朝一个方向向下倾斜，并且可能会在您的脚下开始朝该方向移动。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-038","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-039","input":"使用电池供电的收音机收听当地新闻台的警告。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-039","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-040","input":"始终遵循当地应急管理人员的指示。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-040","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-041","input":"他们根据您社区中的威胁提供最新建议。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-041","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-042","input":"在可能导致山体滑坡的暴风雨中保持警惕和清醒。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-042","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-043","input":"许多人死于山体滑坡是在人们睡觉时发生的。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-043","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-044","input":"请注意，当您确定泥石流即将来临时，再安全逃离就为时已晚。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-044","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-045","input":"切勿过有水或泥流的马路。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-045","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-046","input":"如果您看到有水流逼近，切勿过桥，因为水流会变得越来越大，您无法逃脱。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-046","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-047","input":"如果您确实被困在山体滑坡的路径上，请尽快上坡。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-047","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-048","input":"危险时避开河谷和低洼地带。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-048","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-049","input":"如果您靠近溪流或河道，请注意水流突然增加或减少或水从清澈变为浑浊。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-049","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-050","input":"这些可能是山体滑坡即将来临的迹象。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-050","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-051","input":"额外的载玻片可能会带来危险。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-051","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-052","input":"收听当地电台或电视台的最新紧急信息。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-052","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-053","input":"洪水有时会在山体滑坡和泥石流之后发生，因为它们可能是由相同的条件引发的。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-053","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-054","input":"在不进入直接滑道区域的情况下，检查滑道附近是否有受伤和被困人员。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-054","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-055","input":"引导救援人员到他们的位置。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-055","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-056","input":"向有关当局报告断裂的公用事业线路以及损坏的公路和铁路。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-056","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-057","input":"报告潜在危险将使公用设施尽快关闭，防止进一步的危险和伤害。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-057","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-058","input":"让受过培训的专业人员检查建筑物地基、烟囱和周围土地是否有损坏。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-058","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-059","input":"尽快重新种植受损的土地，因为地面覆盖物丧失造成的侵蚀会在不久的将来导致山洪暴发和更多的山体滑坡。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-059","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-060","input":"向岩土工程专家寻求建议以评估滑坡危害或设计纠正技术以降低滑坡风险。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-060","split":"article"}},{"classification":{"domain":null,"risk":null,"status":"needs_input_only_review"},"id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1/sentence-061","input":"专业人士可以建议您预防或降低山体滑坡风险的最佳方法，而不会造成进一步的危险。","provenance":{"raw_url":"https://www.ready.gov/zh-hans/landslides-debris-flow","source_case_id":"sentence-061","split":"article"}}],"converter_output_used":false,"dataset":"blind-v2","id":"ready-gov-landslides-debris-flow-zh-hans-v1","input_only":true,"license":"U.S. Public Domain","modification_notice":"Extracted only complete Simplified Chinese paragraph and list-item sentences from the checksum-pinned Ready.gov main element, removed navigation, images, external resources, phone/URL instructions, page furniture, and exact duplicates, and added input-only provenance; no expected text or converter output was used.","purpose":"candidate_source_pilot","review_policy":"domain_and_risk_must_be_assigned_from_input_only","source_class":"public_domain","stats":{"by_split":{"article":61},"eligible_pending_review":61,"exclusions":{},"raw_cases":61},"upstream_revision":"Ready.gov Simplified Chinese Landslides and Debris Flow; page last updated 2025-11-12; retrieved HTML SHA-256: f43e3a6e6b0e65d283c735e45d230f0eeac493f3f1dfbaab5b6abd61395088fc","version":1}
